// produceArtifact -- delegate a "make me X" request to the planner (async)
// =========================================================================
//
// The Assistant is the conversational front door. For a request that wants
// something PRODUCED and persisted -- "create a file with the 10 most
// beautiful birds", "put together a one-pager on our refund policy", "export
// a CSV of ..." -- the Assistant does NOT try to author the deliverable inline
// in the chat turn. It calls this tool, which hands the work to the planner
// and returns IMMEDIATELY. The conversation stays fast and asynchronous: the
// planner routes/creates the right specialist, does any research, produces the
// deliverable (default: a markdown file) via the workbench, and lands it in
// the user's Library -- all in the background.
//
// Contrast with a plain QUESTION ("what are the 10 most beautiful birds?"),
// which the Assistant answers inline via respondToUser. The decision rule
// (answer vs produce) lives in the agentReply prompt + the workbench knowledge
// baseline; this tool is the produce-path mechanism.
//
// The handler:
//   1. Mints a v1:planner:plan (kind="produceArtifact", triggerSource=
//      "user.implicit") via the single mutationCreatePlan write path. The
//      desired output format + filename ride in Plan.input so the executing
//      agent knows what to write.
//   2. Returns a small ack payload {status:"delegated", planId, ack}. The
//      Assistant reads it, emits a SHORT respondToUser acknowledgement
//      ("On it -- I'll put that together and drop it in your Library; I'll
//      let you know when it's ready."), and ENDS ITS TURN.
//
// The plan auto-runs (kind="produceArtifact" plans skip the manual Run gate --
// see the planner agent loop's auto-start), so the user never has to visit the
// Tasks page. Completion threads back to the conversation + fires a
// notification (memql#792).
//
// allowedRoles: assistant. Specialists ARE the delegates; they never delegate.
// Mirrors the ensureAgent / requestUserFeedback tool->builtin->integration
// shape (the builtin is integration.agents.produceArtifact in
// dsl/agents/builtins.memql).

@enabled
@handler(type="function", name="produceArtifact")
@allowedRoles("assistant")
@executionTime("fast")
@description("Delegate a PRODUCE request (the user wants a file / document / deliverable created or persisted, not just an answer) to the planner, asynchronously. Returns immediately with a planId. Use this -- NOT an inline answer -- when the user says create / make / build / generate / write / export / save a file, list, doc, report, sheet, etc. Default output is a markdown file in the Library unless the user names another format. After calling it, emit a SHORT acknowledgement via respondToUser and END YOUR TURN; the deliverable lands in the Library in the background. For a plain question the user just wants answered, do NOT call this -- answer inline instead.")
tool produceArtifact {
  goal                 string  @required @description("Self-contained description of the deliverable to produce, phrased as a concrete artifact (e.g. 'A markdown file titled \"10 Most Beautiful Birds\" listing ten birds, each with a one-line description'). The planner reads this verbatim to decompose the work, so name WHAT to make and any specifics the user gave; do not include chit-chat.")
  format               string  @description("Desired output format. Defaults to \"markdown\" when omitted. Set only when the user asked for a specific format (e.g. \"csv\", \"pdf\", \"document\"). The executing agent maps this to the file it writes.")
  filename             string  @description("Optional preferred filename for the deliverable (without path). When omitted the executing agent derives one from the goal.")
  agentId      string  @autoInjected @description("Calling agent id. Server-stamped from the agent runtime; the central validator drops any LLM-supplied value before dispatch.")
  ownerUserId  string  @autoInjected @description("Session-owner user id. Server-stamped; becomes the plan's requestedBy + owner attribution. The central validator drops any LLM-supplied value.")
  spaceId      string  @autoInjected @description("Space the plan lives in. Server-stamped from the agent runtime turn context; the central validator drops any LLM-supplied value.")
}
